          "note": "Cited at its BASE blob because the counterexample IS this version. At 6cba42333d64 `_effect_may_have_occurred` is five lines: read `out.get(\"trace\")`, return False unless it is a list, else return whether any row has a truthy `effect_outcome_sha256`. That is the whole body of the gate that decides `autonomous_replay_authorized = not _effect_may_have_occurred(out)`. Measured with this blob in place, over all 23 benchmark goals driven through `run_raw_goal`: `out[\"trace\"]` is not a list in a single one of them, because the front door nests its trace under `controller_execution`, and `effect_outcome_sha256` never appears anywhere in any result. So the gate returned False for all 23 -- including BENCH_TAR_GZ_CREATE_AND_VERIFY, BENCH_SOURCE_AUDIT_WRITE_JSON, BENCH_MARKDOWN_TO_DECISION, EXT_XLSX_CREATE, EXT_AST_AUDIT and EXT_DECISION_VERIFY, the six that verifiably produced a file and carry `output_sha256` for it, a field absent from every read-only result. A safety gate that cannot locate the evidence reports that no effect occurred, which is failing open, and failing open here means authorizing an autonomous re-run of an action that already wrote to disk. Asking the question the caller actually means -- is there evidence of a produced artifact anywhere in this result -- gives 23 of 23 agreement with ground truth, keeps the legacy shape working, and costs at most 6 milliseconds on the largest result.",
